diff --git a/docs/concurrent-model-services.md b/docs/concurrent-model-services.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f1881db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/concurrent-model-services.md
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+# Concurrent conversation and background project work
+
+## Scope
+
+Optional two-profile local inference: LFM2.5-2.6B for interactive conversation
+and Qwen3.5-4B for project planning and bounded agent decisions. Model names are
+configuration, not hard-coded architecture. The router is disabled by default.
+This patch is standalone against main at 6afda1b; do not apply the earlier
+ASTA-on-demand-model-router.patch first.
+
+Two services do not provide two GPUs. Dual mode allows overlapping HTTP
+inference on separate local llama.cpp servers. It does not guarantee overlapping
+CUDA kernels, a particular response latency, or enough VRAM with speech/vision.
+The coding service starts lazily and stays resident after its first request.
+
+## Operating modes
+
+- `ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER=0`: unchanged legacy single-model provider.
+- `ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER=1`, `ASTA_MODEL_MODE=dual`: independent general/coding
+  service locks, separate client histories and request sessions; one request per
+  profile at a time. Interactive chat/intent JSON always use general, even when
+  a coding task is active. New coding inference waits for existing foreground
+  requests at inference boundaries; active generations are not preempted.
+- `ASTA_MODEL_MODE=on_demand`: explicit low-memory fallback, one text service at
+  a time. Chat can wait behind coding inference in this mode. No automatic
+  unload/retry policy after an OOM: errors remain visible and the user chooses
+  the fallback.
+- `ASTA_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1`: planning and the existing synchronous project
+  tool loop run on a dedicated worker, including approved continuations. One
+  project task only. No new arbitrary shell execution or parallel tool workers.
+
+## Ownership, safety and limitations
+
+Both GGUF paths must be explicit. Endpoints must be distinct loopback HTTP
+ports. A mismatched model identity is rejected. Only ASTA-owned child processes
+are stopped. Dual mode may reuse an externally owned endpoint if its model
+identity matches; its lifecycle belongs to the user. On-demand mode refuses to
+stop an external model in order to switch profiles.
+
+The existing TaskManager has one active slot. While background project work
+owns it, other tool actions and new project tasks are held, not interleaved.
+Read-only conversation, task status and approvals remain available. This is not
+a multi-project agent or concurrent desktop automation implementation.
+
+Existing permissions and critical sandbox approvals remain mandatory. Ordinary
+chat does not cancel a background approval, and bare yes/no cannot authorize it.
+Use the HUD button (request-ID bound), `approve coding step`, or `reject coding
+step`. Approvals still expire according to the existing TTL; expired requests
+cannot execute. Terminal background tasks discard their pending approvals.
+
+`cancel coding task` / `cancel project task` stop future work and remove pending
+approvals. An already-running tool, filesystem operation or sandbox process is
+not forcibly interrupted or rolled back. Do not assume cancellation undoes edits.
+A workspace root change requests cancellation before further background steps.
+Planning/task state is in memory only; tasks do not resume after restart.
+
+The HUD shows both model-service states plus a separate project phase. Background
+progress does not overwrite ordinary listening/speaking state. Approval continues
+to use the existing prominent approval flow. No raw model reasoning is displayed.
+
+## Setup
+
+Close ASTA. Keep the existing CUDA llama-server path in `.env`; use a recent
+llama.cpp build supporting both models and their chat templates. Download:
+
+- `LiquidAI/LFM2.5-2.6B-GGUF`, `LFM2.5-2.6B-Q4_K_M.gguf`
+- `unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF`, `Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf`
+
+Install the optional `huggingface_hub` downloader dependency, then run
+`scripts/download_model_services.py --model-dir PATH`. The checked-in manifest
+pins each download to a repository revision; no model weights are in this patch.
+
+Run `scripts/configure_model_services.py --general PATH --coding PATH`. It updates
+only model-related `.env` keys, removes duplicate selected keys, preserves
+unrelated configuration, and enables the cognitive planner and background work.
+It does not print secrets. `.env` remains ignored. Start with 4K contexts,
+256/128 batch/microbatch and one slot per service. Coding thinking is initially
+disabled for bounded JSON control; benchmark reasoning separately before
+raising context/output budgets. The research benchmarks are not reproduced by
+these conservative settings.
+
+## Acceptance checks
+
+1. Run the focused tests for model router, concurrency, server manager, provider,
+   HUD, workspace tasks and sandbox. They use fakes, not downloaded models.
+2. With ASTA closed, run `python scripts/smoke_concurrent_models.py`. It checks
+   model identities, dual residency and a real chat finishing during coding.
+   It executes no generated code and shuts down only its own servers. Successful
+   output ends with `ASTA_CONCURRENT_MODELS_SMOKE_OK`. Very short coding output
+   may finish too soon to demonstrate overlap; that is reported as inconclusive,
+   not a false positive.
+3. Start ASTA, request an existing supported project task, then ask an unrelated
+   conversational question. Check that chat answers while the project phase
+   remains visible. Check `project task status` and cancel behavior.
+4. At an approval prompt, ask an unrelated question; verify no tool ran. Bare
+   `yes` must not approve background work. Use the request-bound approval button
+   or the explicit phrase, then verify continuation runs on the project worker.
+5. Test memory with speech active and vision loaded when needed; sample
+   `nvidia-smi` peak VRAM and response latency. The model-only smoke omits those
+   resource consumers. If dual residency fails, set `ASTA_MODEL_MODE=on_demand`
+   and use the switching smoke (`scripts/smoke_model_router.py`) instead.
+
+No local Windows/RTX measurement is claimed by the patch. Automated tests prove
+software coordination, not model quality or laptop capacity.
diff --git a/docs/model-router.md b/docs/model-router.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f0adec7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/model-router.md
@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+> This document describes the **on_demand fallback mode**. For dual-model
+> operation and background project work, use [concurrent model services](concurrent-model-services.md).
+> Both modes ship in one standalone patch; the earlier router patch is not required.
+
+# On-demand general/coding model router (V1)
+
+## Scope
+
+The router is opt-in (`ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER=1
+ASTA_MODEL_MODE=on_demand`). Existing single-model behavior is
+unchanged when disabled. It reuses llama.cpp, the provider interface, and the
+existing validated planner/tools; it is not a second agent framework.
+
+V1 uses conservative rules over the original user goal, plus the existing
+workspace task scope. Coding planning and post-action decisions are covered,
+not just ordinary chat. Internal capability descriptions are not classified as
+user intent. An additional LLM classifier is intentionally not implemented yet.
+
+One kernel-scoped runtime owns model-server lifecycles and serializes all text
+inference, including streaming and stateless intent JSON requests. Chat and
+agent clients have separate prompts/histories. Chat history is replayed across
+model switches; task state, approvals, tool results, and verification remain in
+the existing kernel/runtime. A task's role is retained by its in-memory task ID.
+Short coding follow-ups and intent classification can reuse the resident model.
+An unrelated general question can switch back. Nothing automatically resumes a
+previous task or persists model-routing state across restart.
+
+## Setup
+
+Close ASTA normally before changing settings or running the standalone smoke.
+Use an up-to-date CUDA llama.cpp build supporting the existing server flags.
+Download the chosen coding GGUF yourself; ASTA never downloads models at runtime.
+For the initial 8 GB RTX 4060 laptop target, use:
+
+- General: NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf (existing model).
+- Coding baseline: Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf from
+  unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF.
+
+Before placing a second GGUF in the model directory, set the general model path
+explicitly. Automatic single-GGUF discovery becomes ambiguous with two files.
+Add/update the following in the ignored local `.env`, using your actual paths:
+
+```text
+ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER=1
+ASTA_LLM_MODEL_PATH=E:\Projects\llama\models\NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Nano-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_MODEL_PATH=E:\Projects\llama\models\Qwen3.5-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_CONTEXT_SIZE=4096
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_GPU_LAYERS=99
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_BATCH_SIZE=256
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_UBATCH_SIZE=128
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_PARALLEL=1
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_FLASH_ATTN=on
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_REASONING=off
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.6
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=2048
+ASTA_CODING_LLM_MAX_REPLY_SECONDS=120
+ASTA_CODING_AGENT_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=2048
+```
+
+The existing `ASTA_LLAMA_SERVER_PATH` executable is shared. The general endpoint
+remains port 8080. Coding has its own `ASTA_CODING_LLM_*` settings; it does not
+inherit the general model ID, model path, batch sizes, or output budget. An
+optional `ASTA_CODING_LLM_MODEL` alias must match the server's reported model ID.
+Keep both endpoints on loopback HTTP and separate ports. Context includes both
+input and output; these initial settings are for small tasks, not full-repository
+prompts or guaranteed model quality.
+
+If a profile's target files are missing or its endpoint is already occupied by
+an external coding server, reject the switch before unloading the working model.
+ASTA only stops its own child process and confirms exit before starting another.
+An existing matching external general endpoint can be reused, but ASTA refuses
+to unload it for a coding switch. Stop that independently owned server yourself,
+or disable routing. A failed switch never silently uses another model.
+
+Idle optional vision resources use the existing GPU-share release mechanism.
+Active vision, speech GPU usage, unrelated CUDA processes, and display resources
+are not forcibly stopped. Therefore the one-text-model policy is not a guarantee
+that the coding model fits the complete ASTA workload. Measure VRAM and latency
+on the actual laptop. No claim of live GPU validation is made by unit tests.
+
+The HUD shows the requested profile, loading/ready/error status, and model file
+name only. These fields do not overwrite task/approval status and do not display
+hidden reasoning, local model-directory paths, or file contents.
+
+## Validation
+
+```powershell
+.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest -q tests/test_model_router.py tests/test_llm_provider.py tests/test_llama_server_manager.py tests/test_ai_engine.py tests/test_cognitive_planner.py tests/test_workspace_project_task.py tests/test_hud_module.py
+```
+
+With both GGUFs downloaded and ASTA/independent text servers closed:
+
+```powershell
+.venv\Scripts\python scripts/smoke_model_router.py
+```
+
+Expected: general -> coding -> general, only one owned text-server endpoint
+active after each request, ending with `ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER_SMOKE_OK`. This is a
+load/switch smoke, not a coding-correctness test and not the full voice/HUD memory
+budget. It does not execute generated code, register tools, or write project files.
+
+Then start `main.py`, ask an ordinary question, ask a coding question, and ask
+another ordinary question. Verify loading status in the HUD and use `nvidia-smi`
+to record memory with speech/vision present. Finally repeat the small-project
+acceptance task with sandbox approval and observed pytest results. A better
+model does not bypass execution permission or make an unverified task successful.
+
+Rollback: set `ASTA_MODEL_ROUTER=0`, close/restart ASTA. Keep the explicit general
+model path after downloading a second GGUF.
